WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.428
One spring day Robin Hood was watching Little John repair a bow.

2
00:00:06.429 --> 00:00:11.252
The day was warm and pleasant, and Robin felt very content.

3
00:00:11.253 --> 00:00:15.886
"I'd rather live here than in the king's palace," announced Robin.

4
00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:18.556
"The woods are green and beautiful.

5
00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:20.438
Flowers are blooming.

6
00:00:20.439 --> 00:00:23.247
We have plenty of food and fresh water.

7
00:00:23.247 --> 00:00:29.071
There's no better place than Sherwood Forest in springtime."

8
00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:33.813
"Yes, I'm very happy with our life," agreed Little John.

9
00:00:33.814 --> 00:00:37.412
He rubbed the string of his bow with some wax.

10
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:42.437
"You mentioned spring, Robin, but actually, every season has its rewards.

11
00:00:42.438 --> 00:00:48.434
Even winter. Do you remember the winter day we spent with that friar and two beggars?

12
00:00:48.435 --> 00:00:56.282
The friar seemed to be enjoying himself, strolling around the countryside, finding both good food and a warm fire.

13
00:00:56.283 --> 00:01:01.205
If I couldn't live here in Sherwood Forest, I'd like to be a friar."

14
00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:05.121
"Really?" said Robin. "I'd choose to be a beggar.

15
00:01:05.122 --> 00:01:07.979
I thought those two beggars led a happier life.

16
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.785
They told such wonderful stories about meeting people."

17
00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:16.509
Suddenly Robin had an idea. "Let's have an adventure today!

18
00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:19.850
I'll try begging while you try a friar's life.

19
00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:22.282
And then we'll see who has the most fun."

20
00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:27.162
Little John laid down his bow. "Let's do that!"

21
00:01:27.163 --> 00:01:31.513
Robin and his band kept a chest filled with all kinds of clothes.

22
00:01:31.514 --> 00:01:36.361
Little John pulled out a gray friar's robe and put it on.

23
00:01:36.361 --> 00:01:38.737
He tied a string of beads.

24
00:01:38.738 --> 00:01:41.715
Then he went to show Robin and the other men.

25
00:01:41.716 --> 00:01:46.411
Everyone roared with laughter.

26
00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:51.840
The robe was way too short, but Little John didn't care.

27
00:01:51.841 --> 00:01:55.516
He folded his hands in prayer and stared at the ground.

28
00:01:55.516 --> 00:01:59.426
"Do you think I could pass for a humble friar?"

29
00:01:59.427 --> 00:02:04.002
"Never!" Friar Tuck laughed.

30
00:02:04.002 --> 00:02:11.881
"You must look people in the eye, or they'll suspect you're a fraud."

31
00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:15.805
"At least he has a costume," said Robin.

32
00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:20.551
"I'll have to buy clothes from the first beggar I see."

33
00:02:20.552 --> 00:02:25.550
The two men picked up their staffs and set off in different directions.

34
00:02:25.551 --> 00:02:29.229
Little John walked along, whistling happily.

35
00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:34.944
Birds twittered in the trees and green hills rose toward the sky.

36
00:02:34.945 --> 00:02:40.478
Little John soon met three pretty girls, carrying eggs to market.

37
00:02:40.479 --> 00:02:47.179
"Oh, you shouldn't have to carry those heavy baskets," said Little John. "Let me help you."

38
00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.624
"How will you manage all three baskets?" asked the first girl.

39
00:02:51.625 --> 00:02:56.509
"Like this!" Little John handed his staff to the second girl.

40
00:02:56.510 --> 00:03:03.076
Then he tied one basket to his back and carried the other two in his hands.

41
00:03:03.077 --> 00:03:07.249
The girls blushed and giggled.

42
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.282
As the four of them walked toward Nottingham, they made an amusing sight.

43
00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:16.824
Here were three pretty girls with a huge friar in a short robe.

44
00:03:16.824 --> 00:03:21.523
The friar was trying not to drop three baskets of eggs.

45
00:03:21.523 --> 00:03:25.484
People joked with Little John, and he joked right back.

46
00:03:25.484 --> 00:03:29.241
He laughed and talked with the three girls.

47
00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:32.938
"I'm having a great day!" he said to himself.

48
00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:37.170
Little John felt sad when they reached the edge of town.

49
00:03:37.171 --> 00:03:40.265
"I must leave you here," he said.

50
00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:47.524
He didn't dare to enter town—he might meet the sheriff's men!

51
00:03:47.525 --> 00:03:51.869
Little John walked along by himself and reached a little building.

52
00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.423
A sign hung out front with a picture of a stag's head.

53
00:03:55.423 --> 00:04:00.056
"I'm thirsty," he thought. "And that's an inn."

54
00:04:00.057 --> 00:04:04.730
A beggar and a peddler sat outside the inn, having something to drink.

55
00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.537
Two horses were tied to a tree.

56
00:04:08.537 --> 00:04:11.627
"Are those your horses?" asked Little John.

57
00:04:11.628 --> 00:04:17.002
"No, they belong to two friars, who are inside eating.

58
00:04:17.002 --> 00:04:21.238
Would you like to share our drink?" asked the beggar.

59
00:04:21.238 --> 00:04:26.692
"Oh, yes! I've been walking all morning and I'm quite thirsty."

60
00:04:26.693 --> 00:04:31.438
Little John enjoyed a drink and then began to sing.

61
00:04:31.439 --> 00:04:34.397
Soon the two friars came out of the inn.

62
00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:39.253
One friar was tall and thin, and the other was short and fat.

63
00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:43.329
When they heard Little John singing, they both frowned.

64
00:04:43.329 --> 00:04:49.617
"That's not a proper song for a friar to sing," scolded the tall friar.

65
00:04:49.617 --> 00:04:53.409
"You're a disgrace to friars everywhere."

66
00:04:53.409 --> 00:04:56.803
"You know who's a disgrace?" said Little John.

67
00:04:56.804 --> 00:04:59.504
"Friars who cheat the poor."

68
00:04:59.505 --> 00:05:04.055
The beggar and peddler laughed, but the two friars scowled.

69
00:05:04.055 --> 00:05:10.224
As the friars walked toward their horses, Little John offered to help them mount.

70
00:05:10.225 --> 00:05:14.152
"We don't need your help," said the tall friar. "Go away!"

71
00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:16.768
"Oh, no," said Little John.

72
00:05:16.769 --> 00:05:21.124
"I'm sorry that you don't like my company, but I'm a friar too.

73
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:23.388
So I'm coming with you."

74
00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:33.905
The beggar and peddler grinned at the sight—a tall friar in a short robe rushing after two scowling friars.

